{
  "extends": "./tsconfig.node.json",
  "compilerOptions": {
    "composite": false,
    "module": "CommonJS",
    "moduleResolution": "Node",
    "noEmit": true,
    "types": ["node", "jest"],
    // `locale-parity.spec.ts` imports the i18next bundles as JSON. Inherited
    // from `tsconfig.node.json` today, but stated here too: this is the
    // config ts-jest compiles against, and a spec suite should not silently
    // stop building because the build config it extends dropped an option.
    "resolveJsonModule": true
  },
  // One glob per directory `jest.config.js` lists in `roots`, so a new spec
  // is type-checked the moment it exists. This was a file-by-file allowlist,
  // which is a silent failure mode for a config whose whole job is to tell
  // you whether things are checked: `scripts/verify-local-only-ai-in-package.spec.ts`
  // reported clean while sitting outside the program entirely, and the only
  // reason it was noticed was someone reading this list.
  //
  // `src/main` and `scripts` are whole-directory globs: both are
  // node-targeted, so every file in them belongs in this program.
  //
  // `src/renderer/lib` is `*.spec.ts` only, and that is not a hedge. The
  // directory holds browser-targeted modules beside the tested ones --
  // `api-client.ts` reads `import.meta.env` and `window`, `category-label.ts`
  // and `use-chatgpt-status.ts` import `.tsx` -- which belong to
  // `tsconfig.web.json`'s program and produce 14 errors in a node one with no
  // DOM lib and no `--jsx`. Pulling the whole renderer in here is a separate,
  // larger problem and widening this glob is not how to solve it. The modules
  // the specs do exercise still land in the program, by import resolution,
  // exactly as they did when they were listed by hand.
  //
  // `src/preload` and `src/shared` are not jest roots and hold no spec; they
  // are here because `src/main` imports them, and naming them keeps that
  // dependency checked rather than merely pulled in.
  "include": [
    "src/main/**/*.ts",
    "src/preload/**/*.ts",
    "src/shared/**/*.ts",
    "src/renderer/lib/**/*.spec.ts",
    "scripts/**/*.ts",
    "src/renderer/i18n/locales/en.json",
    "src/renderer/i18n/locales/pt.json"
  ],
  "exclude": ["node_modules"]
}
